<http://data.silknow.org/object/e5bba1c1-0256-30ee-8052-e7bbc5d90a9a>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Man's waistcoat, 1780-85, British; yellow and black striped silk, silver braid, double-breasted"@en , "Man's waistcoat with round neckline, curving fronts and skirts reaching to the top of the thigh.  Each front has a welted pocket.  The fronts are made of silk with narrow stripes of black satin and yellow twill; the back of brown worsted twill.  The waistcoat is lined with unbleached fustian; the fronts faced and skirts lined with golden-brown silk twill.  The front necks, fronts, hems and pocket welts are edged with a 7mm-wide lace (braid) of woven silk and silver thread.  There re 14 worked buttonholes along the left front and 14 corresponding buttons covered with silver-gilt thread on the right front.  An additional 13 ubttons are sewn to the left proper of the buttonholes, giving a double-breasted effect.  The bottom button and buttonhole are single-breasted and the front edges stepped for the overlap above."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/6fab69e9-d383-3f66-867f-3efa13532c71> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/ea43b9db-00a0-38ab-ad8a-7e11bc3f9a3b> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/d7585ddd-ac1c-3010-9d57-f5fae358bb9f> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/6b0a25d8-e495-315c-95b4-bf1812ea1b5b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Man's waistcoat with round neckline, curving fronts and skirts reaching to the top of the thigh.  Each front has a welted pocket.  The fronts are made of silk with narrow stripes of black satin and yellow twill; the back of brown worsted twill.  The waistcoat is lined with unbleached fustian; the fronts faced and skirts lined with golden-brown silk twill.  The front necks, fronts, hems and pocket welts are edged with a 7mm-wide lace (braid) of woven silk and silver thread.  There re 14 worked buttonholes along the left front and 14 corresponding buttons covered with silver-gilt thread on the right front.  An additional 13 ubttons are sewn to the left proper of the buttonholes, giving a double-breasted effect.  The bottom button and buttonhole are single-breasted and the front edges stepped for the overlap above."@en , "Man's waistcoat, 1780-85, British; yellow and black striped silk, silver braid, double-breasted"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/e5bba1c1-0256-30ee-8052-e7bbc5d90a9a/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/e5bba1c1-0256-30ee-8052-e7bbc5d90a9a/dimension/1> ;
