        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Man's waistcoat with round neckline, curving fronts and skirts reaching to the top of the thigh.  Each front has a welted pocket.  The fronts are made of silk with narrow stripes of black satin and yellow twill; the back of brown worsted twill.  The waistcoat is lined with unbleached fustian; the fronts faced and skirts lined with golden-brown silk twill.  The front necks, fronts, hems and pocket welts are edged with a 7mm-wide lace (braid) of woven silk and silver thread.  There re 14 worked buttonholes along the left front and 14 corresponding buttons covered with silver-gilt thread on the right front.  An additional 13 ubttons are sewn to the left proper of the buttonholes, giving a double-breasted effect.  The bottom button and buttonhole are single-breasted and the front edges stepped for the overlap above."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e5bba1c1-0256-30ee-8052-e7bbc5d90a9a> .

